{"nodes": [{"id": "godot_port_design_doc", "label": "Godot 4 port design doc", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L1-14", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Merges this repo's actual content and visual system with the engineering patterns (Autoloads, JSON content, node-per-mechanic, performance discipline) of an uploaded Godot example doc, while discarding that doc's curriculum and grade-banded level concepts."}, {"id": "godot_example_doc", "label": "Uploaded Godot example doc (e41a819a-cyberwellnessgamedesigndoc.md)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L10", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "godot_revision_note", "label": "Revision note: replace bin-heavy mechanics", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L14", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The original draft kept Sort/Sort/Spot/Balance, three of which are variations on 'put things in a bin' - flat once it is an actual game instead of a web form; so a platformer and a stepping-stone run were borrowed from the example doc while Bully Bog's Sort and Balance Bay's Balance stayed."}, {"id": "godot_decision_stay_2d", "label": "Decision: stay 2D, not 3D", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L18-25", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two independent reasons: the example doc's performance section rules out 3D for this audience/hardware (target the oldest laptop in the room), and this game's identity IS 2D paper-journal illustration, so 3D would fight the 'internet as a place worth exploring' rationale. Extra depth comes from parallax layers, an ink-bleed shader, and capped GPUParticles2D instead."}, {"id": "godot_principle_no_fail_state", "label": "Principle 1: no fail state (Godot)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L33", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Decision scenes never queue_free() on a wrong pick; they swap the dialogue label and re-enable the choice buttons."}, {"id": "godot_principle_mechanic_is_lesson", "label": "Principle 2: the mechanic is the lesson", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L34", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Winning must require doing the safe behaviour, not just be themed around it - hence the platformer meter is built from real character-type mixing and the river stones are the actual scam scenarios, not decoration around an unrelated jumping puzzle."}, {"id": "godot_principle_four_mechanics", "label": "Principle 3: four mechanics, one per realm", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L35", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deliberately trades design.md's 'fewer controls to learn' for 'each realm feels distinct', judged worth it once this is a real game rather than a form."}, {"id": "godot_principle_nothing_is_villain", "label": "Principle 4: nothing is a villain", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L36", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Keeper Vex, the Fog and the Glimmer are misguided-not-malicious; the dialogue tone must survive the port verbatim."}, {"id": "godot_principle_no_data_collection", "label": "Principle 5: no login, no data collection", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L37", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only a first name held in memory today; Godot save data must stay local-only to keep this intact."}, {"id": "godot_realm_anatomy", "label": "Realm anatomy (Realm.tscn node layout)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L57-78", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every realm is one .tscn with the same internal state machine driven by JSON content instead of hardcoded dialogue; Bully Bog and Balance Bay keep the four-phase shape while Passworld and Privacy Peaks fold decision into the mini-game."}, {"id": "godot_realm_state_machine", "label": "RealmState machine (idle to story to game to rule to stamped)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L70-77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "godot_walk_system_port", "label": "Walk system port (useWalker.js to CharacterBody2D)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L80-87", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The current walker is already exactly Godot's CharacterBody2D pattern: _physics_process replaces the rAF loop, Input.get_vector() replaces the KEY_DIRS table, and a clicked point sets a target Vector2 mirroring walkTo(); 0-100 world units stay resolution-independent with one scalar per realm."}, {"id": "godot_hotspots", "label": "Hotspots as Area2D stops", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L89-91", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each realm's four named stops become Area2D nodes with a label and action verb; RealmState enables only the hotspot relevant to the current phase, the same gating RealmScreen does in React today."}, {"id": "godot_minigame_platformer", "label": "Password Fortress platformer (Passworld)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L102", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A strength meter fills only from a mix of letter/number/symbol tiles, and decoy tiles shaped like weak passwords (123456, password) are easy to reach but reduce the meter - teaching 'looks like a password, isn't a strong one' the way the old Sort game's bins taught 'looks shareable, isn't'. A patrolling hacker knocks the player back to the section start: momentum lost, not a life."}, {"id": "godot_minigame_river_run", "label": "Cross the Fog stepping-stone run (Privacy Peaks)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L107", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Merges the old decision card and the separate Clear the Fog spot game into one phase; the six existing messages map one-to-one onto six stones, and two of them are genuinely fine so the run does not train 'every stranger message is a trap'. Wrong picks wobble the stone and produce a soft splash, not a drowning, then re-offer the same stone."}, {"id": "godot_minigame_sort", "label": "Clear the Water sort (Bully Bog, unchanged)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L113", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Immediate per-item feedback rather than end-of-round scoring, matching design.md's no-score-pressure rule."}, {"id": "godot_minigame_balance", "label": "Balance the Day (Balance Bay, unchanged)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L119", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "6 slots filled from 10 cards with no single correct split - only all-screen or no-screen trip a verdict, and a level mix reads as 'that's the whole trick'."}, {"id": "godot_keeper_vex", "label": "Keeper Vex (Passworld character)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L100-101", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "godot_the_fog", "label": "The Fog (Privacy Peaks antagonist)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L106", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "godot_pockets", "label": "Pockets (Bully Bog character)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L111-112", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "godot_the_glimmer", "label": "The Glimmer (Balance Bay character)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L117-118", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "godot_travelers_pledge", "label": "Traveler's Pledge (finale, four lines)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L122-126", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "godot_json_content_pattern", "label": "Content lives in JSON, not GDScript", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L143-146", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Called the example doc's strongest idea and taken wholesale, so dialogue and realm bounds are authored data rather than code."}, {"id": "godot_journey_manager", "label": "journey_manager autoload", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L164-191", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Holds traveler name, current screen and the realm_progress dictionary carried over unchanged from design.md section 7; set up first so every realm scene can read what has been earned without re-wiring signals scene-to-scene."}, {"id": "godot_stamp_manager", "label": "stamp_manager autoload", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L165-178", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "godot_project_layout", "label": "res:// project layout (scenes/scripts/data/assets)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L147-176", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "godot_save_system", "label": "Local FileAccess save system", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L195-197", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A Godot build is a real client and can persist for free, so a small local JSON save at user:// is framed as a genuine upgrade from the port rather than scope creep - it stores nothing beyond the first name already collected, keeping Principle 5 intact."}, {"id": "godot_visual_system_port", "label": "Visual system ported token-for-token", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L201-214", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "design.md section 3 tokens map onto Theme panel background, Theme font colors, per-realm realm_accent export vars, and three DynamicFont resources - explicitly ported rather than reinterpreted."}, {"id": "godot_ink_stamp_badge_port", "label": "Ink stamp badge in Godot (Path2D arc label, baked jitter)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L214", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Per-vertex circle jitter is baked once rather than randomized at runtime, and the +/-6 degree rotation is set once on stamp-earned and never re-rolled, to match design.md's 'randomized once per session'."}, {"id": "godot_motion_budget", "label": "Godot motion budget (two moments)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L216-220", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Godot has no direct prefers-reduced-motion equivalent, so a skippable/instant page-fold would need a manual settings toggle if it matters enough to add."}, {"id": "godot_accessibility_bar", "label": "Godot accessibility & kid-safety bar", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L224-230", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "godot_distribution_html5", "label": "HTML5 export as primary distribution target", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L234-238", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This is a browser game today with no offline/classroom requirement in the repo docs, unlike the example doc's school-laptop .exe scenario; native export stays an easy later addition but nothing should be built around requiring it."}, {"id": "godot_build_order", "label": "Suggested build order (cheapest mechanic first)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L242-253", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sequenced by mechanical complexity: Bully Bog goes first (not Passworld) because a plain Control-based Sort validates the walk system, hotspot gating, dialogue cards, stamp thunk and page-fold at lowest risk; the platformer is last because it is the only mechanic needing real collision, camera follow and game-feel playtesting."}, {"id": "godot_open_questions", "label": "Open questions (save, audio, milestone scope, difficulty, stone count)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L257-263", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Explicitly left undecided: persistence vs session-only parity, audio vs silence, vertical slice vs all four realms, a difficulty pass for the platformer, and whether six river stones exceed the example doc's 4-5 scenario budget."}], "edges": [{"source": "godot_port_design_doc", "target": "godot_example_doc", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L10", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "godot_port_design_doc", "target": "design_concept_summary", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L9", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "godot_port_design_doc", "target": "readme_cyber_wellness_quest", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L4, L269", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "godot_decision_stay_2d", "target": "design_field_journal_metaphor", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L23", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "godot_decision_stay_2d", "target": "godot_example_doc", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L22", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "godot_revision_note", "target": "godot_principle_four_mechanics", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L14-35", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "godot_revision_note", "target": "godot_minigame_platformer", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L14", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "godot_revision_note", "target": "godot_minigame_river_run", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L14", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "godot_principle_four_mechanics", "target": "design_minigame_sort", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "godot.md", "source_location": "L35"